  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:5745",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways, all ultimately targeting the coronary artery smooth muscle cell line. The first pathway involves the tyrosine-protein kinase Blk, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, and the second pathway involves the serine/threonine-protein kinase TAO1, targeted by K-252a. The third pathway links Theasaponin E1 to Placenta growth factor, which is also targeted by K-252a. While these pathways are distinct, they all converge on the coronary artery smooth muscle cell line through the shared target K-252a. This suggests that Theasaponin E1 may act through different kinases to modulate cellular processes that influence the coronary artery smooth muscle cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Theasaponin E1 to exert its effects through multiple molecular mechanisms, potentially involving diverse signaling pathways that regulate smooth muscle function.",
